{
  "verdict": "revise",
  "issues": [
    "Scope: The answer reports a weighted, segment‑adjusted difference (0.1307) instead of the simple overall difference on completed orders; it also fails to exclude the six internal QA orders that remain in the data.",
    "Grounding: The segment‑level conversion rates and the weighted calculation are not present in the printed output, which only shows overall rates (email 0.3879, paid_search 0.3134, diff 0.0745).",
    "Overreach: The answer makes a causal claim (“email campaign improved conversion”) despite the channel not being randomly assigned and only observational adjustment for one confounder.",
    "Unacknowledged data problems: The analyst did not remove the high‑revenue QA orders (identified by revenue > $50,000) and ignored the sentinel -1 values in customer_age, both flagged in the data description."
  ]
}
